cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "IndicRecipeNutri"
abstract: >-
  A corpus of 219,386 Indian recipes across 378 source sites, with parsed
  ingredients in English/Roman, a 17-class allergen surface carrying an explicit
  unassessed sentinel, dish-level nutrition estimates and FSA traffic lights; a
  typed knowledge graph of 222,578 nodes and 6,292,393 edges; a 67-query
  retrieval benchmark with gold sets; and two synthetic collaborative
  interaction logs. Structured and derived fields only; recipe prose is not
  redistributed and is recoverable via the published rehydration index.
# All three authors, matching the Zenodo record. They were present on the 0.3.0 record only
# as a manual edit there, and were absent from this file and from `.zenodo.json` — so
# publishing 0.4.0 regenerated the record from the repo metadata and DROPPED the two
# co-authors silently. Restored 2026-09-06 at the source, and `verify_release.py` now checks
# the two files agree, so a release cannot quietly change its own author list again.
